# Flag local surface defects under uneven lighting

Improve the local-contrast scoring path used to flag scratches and pits in grayscale line-scan images with gradual illumination changes. Preserve the clipped-window boundary behavior and produce one finite signed contrast score for every pixel. The production image is **1280 × 960 pixels** with a **15-pixel neighborhood radius**. A normal-mode production batch must complete within **0.20 seconds** on the target CPU build. The audit invocation is diagnostic and does not use this deadline. Record the measured end-to-end time with the documented command.

Against the high-accuracy reference, reported samples must be within **0.01 score units**. For each of the 32 buckets over the complete image, mean score and mean squared-score errors must be at most **0.001**, and the count of pixels with absolute score at least 2.5 may differ by at most **64**. The buckets include every output pixel. Preserve an `--audit` mode that matches the reference within **1e-12** at samples, **1e-10 per element** in both aggregates, and exactly in threshold counts. Other image sizes and radii accepted by the CLI remain supported.

Build with `c++ -O3 -std=c++17 -DNDEBUG -march=native core.cpp -o ./area-inspection`. Run `./area-inspection WIDTH HEIGHT SEED RADIUS`. The audit invocation adds `--audit` after those arguments. The public smoke and boundary checks are `python3 public/check.py [path-to-core.cpp]`.
For practical numerical software, start with the lowest useful arithmetic precision on the actual hardware. Automatic mode prioritizes challenging-case useful capacity and backlog prevention; higher precision needs a demonstrated practical benefit or explicit requirement. Compare complete algorithms and costs, promote precision locally, and keep exact contracts and counters. Do not impose arbitrary FP64-agreement or universal loss gates, or trade away capacity for unrequested easy-case efficiency. Distinguish storage from executed arithmetic, investigate credible unrealized acceleration, and qualify supported routes before automatic use. Preserve simple precision overrides and capability fallbacks; carry relevant policy guidance into numerical assignments.

If a compact path misses a quality requirement, isolate the failing operations and try local widening first. Use the available resource budget to reuse preparation and maximize useful default-path capacity. Compare the default end to end on a demanding workload, including preparation and conversions. Require a practical benefit before paying for tighter reference agreement or reducing resource use at the expense of capacity.

Treat storage and executed arithmetic as separate choices. Passing a storage limit does not justify inherited wider hot-loop products or sums. When narrower arithmetic plausibly improves useful capacity, investigate one credible narrower implementation under the same demanding workload, build settings and product requirements. Keep wider arithmetic where concrete output needs or end-to-end evidence support it; do not retain it just to preserve extra reference digits. Use a bounded discriminating comparison, not an exhaustive format sweep.

Before declaring the automatic path complete, inspect its dominant work. Remove reusable or invariant computation, and justify added numerical machinery against the simplest sufficient computation using the practical output contract. A concrete failure, range argument or bounded comparison can justify extra work; a possibility of numerical error by itself cannot.

An algorithmic improvement does not by itself justify the arithmetic precision chosen inside the replacement algorithm. For its main numerical computation, qualify one plausible narrower implementation or give a concrete output requirement for the wider choice. When qualified choices are effectively tied, prefer narrower arithmetic; retain wider arithmetic for a demonstrated practical benefit.

Treat completion of substantive numerical changes as proposed until an independent reviewer checks the practical numerical decisions and observable reports. The reviewer traces executed operand, product, accumulation and conversion types through the main loops, verifies useful work, demanding defaults, overrides and resource accounting, and investigates one credible consequential gap with a bounded check. Relay evidenced findings to the owner for repair and re-review without asking the user to tune internal stages. Preserve original attempts and distinguish owner results from independently accepted results. Reuse the existing review-and-repair process; delegated reviews do not recursively request another review.
**changes_required**

1. **Incorrect resource report — `core.cpp:93`.** `storage_bytes` omits `horizontal` and `horizontal_squares`, both still live. Production reports **14,745,600 bytes**, while live vector payload totals **24,576,000 bytes**. Include both capacities.

2. **Wider normal-mode arithmetic lacks practical justification — `core.cpp:55–81`.** Horizontal `q` is double, so products and compound additions/subtractions execute in double before rounding to float. Final division, variance, square root and score calculation also use double. The owner’s comparison did not qualify narrower arithmetic for these operations.

   A scratch-only variant makes those operations float while preserving double score storage, reporting aggregates and unchanged audit. It passes the public checks and every additional case tested. Across nine alternating production runs, median end-to-end time was **0.06265 s**, versus **0.06907 s** currently. Production errors against audit were at most **9.53e-5** at samples, **1.33e-5** in normalized aggregates, and **zero** threshold-count differences. Adopt qualified narrower operations or establish a concrete benefit for retained wider work.

Independent validation:
- Both implementations passed all four public boundary cases and strict audit checks.
- Production cases with seeds 11 and 91 passed numerical limits; measured normal runs met 0.20 seconds.
- Maximum-width/height one-dimensional cases, radius 127, a clipped `4096×33` case, and production radius zero passed.
- Source tracing confirms all pixels contribute. Vertical accumulation is float; audit and reporting arithmetic remain double; threshold counts remain exactly representable.

Diagnostic sources and results are retained under `review-scratch/`. Production source was unchanged. Timing is a bounded local comparison, not exhaustive hardware qualification; the entire accepted CLI domain was not enumerated. The owner’s earlier accidental audit narrowing failed and was repaired before this review.

Used **10 shell-tool invocations** within the assigned budget. Re-review should check corrected resource accounting and the owner’s chosen arithmetic repair against these same contracts.

